    <statement><p><p>The table shows the time, <m>t</m> minutes, that <m>{55}</m> learners spent on homework one evening.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Time (minutes)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20} \le {t} \lt {30}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{30} \le {t} \lt {40}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{40} \le {t} \lt {50}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{50} \le {t} \lt {60}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{60} \le {t} \lt {70}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{70} \le {t} \lt {80}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Frequency (<m>f</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{15}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{14}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>Use the class midpoints, <m>x</m>.</p><p>(a) Find <m>\Sigma fx</m>.</p><div><m>\Sigma fx =</m> <fillin characters="7" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find <m>\Sigma fx^2</m>.</p><div><m>\Sigma fx^2 =</m> <fillin characters="9" name="ans2"/>  </div><p>(c) Estimate the mean, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><div><m>\bar{x} =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans3"/> minutes  </div><p>(d) Estimate the standard deviation, correct to 2 decimal places. Do not round until the final answer.</p><div><m>\sigma =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans4"/> minutes  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Grouped data do not give the exact values, so we place every value at the midpoint of its class. The mean and standard deviation found this way are estimates.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Class</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Frequency (<m>f</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Midpoint (<m>x</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>fx</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>fx^2</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20} \le {t} \lt {30}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{25}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{125}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3125}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{30} \le {t} \lt {40}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{35}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{175}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6125}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{40} \le {t} \lt {50}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{45}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{450}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20\,250}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{50} \le {t} \lt {60}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{15}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{55}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{825}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{45\,375}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{60} \le {t} \lt {70}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{14}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{65}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{910}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{59\,150}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{70} \le {t} \lt {80}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{75}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{450}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{33\,750}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Total</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{55}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2935}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{167\,775}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>(a) <m>\Sigma fx = {2935}</m>. (b) <m>\Sigma fx^2 = {167\,775}</m>.</p><p>(c) <me>\bar{x} = \frac{\Sigma fx}{\Sigma f} = \frac{ {2935} }{ {55} } \approx {53.4}</me></p><p>(d) The variance is the mean of the squares minus the square of the mean. Keep <m>\bar{x}</m> unrounded: <me>\sigma^2 = \frac{\Sigma fx^2}{\Sigma f} - \bar{x}^2 = \frac{ {167\,775} }{ {55} } - {53.364}^2 \approx {202.777}</me>so <m>\sigma = \sqrt{\sigma^2} \approx {14.24}</m> minutes, the standard deviation in the units of the data.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>2935</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>167775</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{587}{11}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{2 \sqrt{6134}}{11}</m></p></answer>
